            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic congestion syndrome--findings on multi-detector row computerized tomography: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>569-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic pelvic pain is a common gynecologic complaint, sometimes without any obvious etiology. We report a case of pelvic congestion syndrome with chronic pelvic pain. The diagnosis can be overlooked by clinical physicians but diagnosed using multi-detector row computerized tomography. This method seems to be an effective and non-invasive imaging modality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
